 by: Appendix C,\n2174\tIntroduction,\n2175\tUnified and Autoregressively Predictable Speech Tokens.\n2176\t\n2177\tYe et al. (2025b)\n2178\tZ. Ye, X. Zhu, C. Chan, X. Wang, X. Tan, J. Lei, Y. Peng, H. Liu, Y. Jin, Z. Dai, et al.\n2179\t\n2180\tLlasa: scaling train-time and inference-time compute for Llama-based speech synthesis.\n2181\t\n2182\tExternal Links: 2502.04128,\n2183\tLink\n2184\t\n2185\tCited by: Appendix C,\n2186\tIntroduction,\n2187\tIntroduction,\n2188\tUnified and Autoregressively Predictable Speech Tokens.\n2189\t\n2190\tZeghidour et al. (2022)\n2191\tN. Zeghidour, A. Luebs, A. Omran, J. Skoglund, and M. Tagliasacchi\n2192\t\n2193\tSoundStream: an end-to-end neural audio codec.\n2194\t\n2195\tIEEE/ACM Transactions on Audio, Speech, and Language Processing 30, pp. 495–507.\n2196\t\n2197\tExternal Links: Document\n2198\t\n2199\tCited by: Appendix C.\n2200\t\n2201\tZhang et al. (2024)\n2202\tX. Zhang, D. Zhang, S. Li, Y. Zhou, and X. Qiu\n2203\t\n2204\tSpeechTokenizer: unified speech tokenizer for speech language models.\n2205\t\n2206\tIn International Conference on Learning Representations,\n2207\t\n2208\tCited by: Appendix C,\n2209\tAppendix C,\n2210\tIntroduction,\n2211\tStructured Semantic–Acoustic Speech Representations.\n2212\t\n2213\t \n2214\t\n2215\t Experimental support, please\n2216\t view the build logs\n2217\t for errors. Generated by\n2218\t \n2219\t \n2220\t L\n2221\t A\n2222\t T\n2223\t E\n2224\t \n2225\t xml\n2226\t \n2227\t .\n2228\t \n2229\t\n2230\t \n2231\t\n2232\t \n2233\tInstructions for reporting errors\n2234\t\n2235\t \n2236\tWe are continuing to improve HTML versions of papers, and your feedback helps enhance accessibility and mobile\n2237\t support. To report errors in the HTML that will help us improve conversion and rendering, choose any of the\n2238\t methods listed below:\n2239\t\n2240\t \n2241\t \n2242\tClick the \"Report Issue\" (\n2243\t \n2244\t ) button, located in the page header.\n2245\t \n2246\t \n2247\tTip: You can