{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-8ef5a8ac127296dd", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# SACodec: Asymmetric Quantization with Semantic Anchoring for Low-Bitrate High-Fidelity Neural Speech Codecs\narXiv: 2512.20944\nAuthors: Zhongren Dong, Bin Wang, Jing Han, Haotian Guo, Xiaojun Mo, Yimin Cao, Zixing Zhang\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: codec_vae\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. A semantic anchoring mechanism leverages a fixed mHuBERT codebook aligned via a lightweight projector to inject semantic priors while preventing codebook collapse.\n  2. A residual activation module equips a single-layer VQ with SimVQ to guarantee full codebook activation for fine-grained acoustic detail recovery.\n  3. SACodec establishes a new state of the art at 1.5 kbps by simultaneously achieving superior acoustic reconstruction fidelity and stronger semantic representation in downstream tasks.\n\nTags: 压缩, 压缩/量化-VQ, 压缩/语义声学-语义, 压缩/语义声学-声学", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "89fad903-2b86-4ac0-bb38-18cb15a4f47a", "uuid": "981777c8-8422-47e8-80be-ecf8a3c298eb", "timestamp": "2026-08-12T04:11:13.894Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# SACodec: Asymmetric Quantization with Semantic Anchoring for Low-Bitrate High-Fidelity Neural Speech Codecs\narXiv: 2512.20944\nAuthors: Zhongren Dong, Bin Wang, Jing Han, Haotian Guo, Xiaojun Mo, Yimin Cao, Zixing Zhang\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: codec_vae\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. A semantic anchoring mechanism leverages a fixed mHuBERT codebook aligned via a lightweight projector to inject semantic priors while preventing codebook collapse.\n  2. A residual activation module equips a single-layer VQ with SimVQ to guarantee full codebook activation for fine-grained acoustic detail recovery.\n  3. SACodec establishes a new state of the art at 1.5 kbps by simultaneously achieving superior acoustic reconstruction fidelity and stronger semantic representation in downstream tasks.\n\nTags: 压缩, 压缩/量化-VQ, 压缩/语义声学-语义, 压缩/语义声学-声学", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-be6af368db2a3ad4", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# NaturalSpeech 3: Zero-Shot Speech Synthesis with Factorized Codec and Diffusion Models\narXiv: 2403.03100\nAuthors: Zeqian Ju, Yuancheng Wang, Kai Shen, Xu Tan, Detai Xin, Dongchao Yang, Yanqing Liu, Yichong Leng, Kaitao Song, Siliang Tang, Zhizheng Wu, Tao Qin, Xiang-Yang Li, Wei Ye, Shikun Zhang, Jiang Bian, Lei He, Jinyu Li, Sheng Zhao\nYear: 2024 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. A novel neural speech codec with factorized vector quantization is proposed to disentangle speech waveforms into distinct subspaces of content, prosody, timbre, and acoustic details.\n  2. A factorized diffusion model is introduced to generate speech attributes in each disentangled subspace following their corresponding prompts in a divide-and-conquer manner.\n  3. The system achieves state-of-the-art performance and human-level naturalness on the multi-speaker LibriSpeech dataset for zero-shot text-to-speech synthesis.\n  4. The factorization design enables flexible speech attribute manipulation by allowing different prompts to control different attributes independently.\n  5. The effectiveness of the system is further improved by scaling the model to 1 billion parameters and the training data to 200K hours.\n\nTags: TTS, 压缩, TTS/架构-NAR-Diffusion, TTS/控制-参考语音, 压缩/量化-VQ, 压缩/语义声学-语义, 压缩/语义声学-声学, 压缩/语义声学-混合", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "89fad903-2b86-4ac0-bb38-18cb15a4f47a", "uuid": "e9f01be0-5c3a-40d9-a71c-644be14aaccc", "timestamp": "2026-08-12T04:11:14.148Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# NaturalSpeech 3: Zero-Shot Speech Synthesis with Factorized Codec and Diffusion Models\narXiv: 2403.03100\nAuthors: Zeqian Ju, Yuancheng Wang, Kai Shen, Xu Tan, Detai Xin, Dongchao Yang, Yanqing Liu, Yichong Leng, Kaitao Song, Siliang Tang, Zhizheng Wu, Tao Qin, Xiang-Yang Li, Wei Ye, Shikun Zhang, Jiang Bian, Lei He, Jinyu Li, Sheng Zhao\nYear: 2024 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. A novel neural speech codec with factorized vector quantization is proposed to disentangle speech waveforms into distinct subspaces of content, prosody, timbre, and acoustic details.\n  2. A factorized diffusion model is introduced to generate speech attributes in each disentangled subspace following their corresponding prompts in a divide-and-conquer manner.\n  3. The system achieves state-of-the-art performance and human-level naturalness on the multi-speaker LibriSpeech dataset for zero-shot text-to-speech synthesis.\n  4. The factorization design enables flexible speech attribute manipulation by allowing different prompts to control different attributes independently.\n  5. The effectiveness of the system is further improved by scaling the model to 1 billion parameters and the training data to 200K hours.\n\nTags: TTS, 压缩, TTS/架构-NAR-Diffusion, TTS/控制-参考语音, 压缩/量化-VQ, 压缩/语义声学-语义, 压缩/语义声学-声学, 压缩/语义声学-混合", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
