{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-96f12bc763718b55", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# On the Distillation Loss Functions of Speech VAE for Unified Reconstruction, Understanding, and Generation\narXiv: 2604.12383\nAuthors: Changhao Cheng, Wei Wang, Wangyou Zhang, Dongya Jia, Jian Wu, Zhuo Chen, Yanmin Qian\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: codec_vae\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Systematic exploration of different distillation loss functions for speech VAEs aligned with foundation models across reconstruction, understanding, and generation tasks.\n  2. Introduction of a dimension-wise distillation scheme that captures temporal structure and local feature variations.\n  3. Formulation of a joint-marginal alignment approach that enforces intra-distribution consistency between VAE latents and foundation model features via frame-level and sequence-level losses.\n  4. Development of an adaptive weighting strategy that dynamically balances reconstruction and alignment losses based on gradient norms.\n  5. Demonstration that the joint-marginal alignment with adaptive weighting achieves the best overall balance and performance across reconstruction, understanding, and generation.\n  6. Analysis revealing that frame-wise alignment primarily captures semantic information for understanding, while sequence-level alignment preserves acoustic information for reconstruction and generation.\n\nTags: 压缩, 压缩/量化-VAE, SSL", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "89fad903-2b86-4ac0-bb38-18cb15a4f47a", "uuid": "cbfae611-b2e9-406f-8798-c995287efa04", "timestamp": "2026-08-12T04:12:46.538Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# On the Distillation Loss Functions of Speech VAE for Unified Reconstruction, Understanding, and Generation\narXiv: 2604.12383\nAuthors: Changhao Cheng, Wei Wang, Wangyou Zhang, Dongya Jia, Jian Wu, Zhuo Chen, Yanmin Qian\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: codec_vae\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Systematic exploration of different distillation loss functions for speech VAEs aligned with foundation models across reconstruction, understanding, and generation tasks.\n  2. Introduction of a dimension-wise distillation scheme that captures temporal structure and local feature variations.\n  3. Formulation of a joint-marginal alignment approach that enforces intra-distribution consistency between VAE latents and foundation model features via frame-level and sequence-level losses.\n  4. Development of an adaptive weighting strategy that dynamically balances reconstruction and alignment losses based on gradient norms.\n  5. Demonstration that the joint-marginal alignment with adaptive weighting achieves the best overall balance and performance across reconstruction, understanding, and generation.\n  6. Analysis revealing that frame-wise alignment primarily captures semantic information for understanding, while sequence-level alignment preserves acoustic information for reconstruction and generation.\n\nTags: 压缩, 压缩/量化-VAE, SSL", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
